WEBVTT

1
01:13:16.906 --> 01:13:18.906
We are going to begin with God's Word.

2
01:13:19.906 --> 01:13:27.906
Last Thursday we celebrated Ascension together worldwide.

3
01:13:27.906 --> 01:13:38.906
And when Jesus rises from the dead, the Bible says he walks around for 40 days to reveal himself,

4
01:13:38.906 --> 01:13:44.906
to show himself to the people that he has truly risen.

5
01:13:44.906 --> 01:13:49.906
What I see here from both Matthew and also in Acts,

6
01:13:49.906 --> 01:13:54.906
is that Jesus takes his disciples on some sort of tour.

7
01:13:54.906 --> 01:14:01.906
For in Matthew chapter 28, the story of the Ascension is not actually there.

8
01:14:01.906 --> 01:14:07.906
Matthew chapter 28 ends with the Great Commission, that is what I will talk about today.

9
01:14:07.906 --> 01:14:11.906
Matthew 28 verse 19 says the following words.

10
01:14:11.906 --> 01:14:16.906
Go therefore and make disciples of all nations.

11
01:14:16.906 --> 01:14:20.906
Baptize them in the name of the Father and the Son and the Holy Spirit.

12
01:14:20.906 --> 01:14:22.906
We always do this in the baptismal water, do you know that?

13
01:14:22.906 --> 01:14:27.906
And teach them to do everything that I have commanded you.

14
01:14:27.906 --> 01:14:33.906
And some people then think to themselves, this is the moment when Jesus ascends to heaven.

15
01:14:33.906 --> 01:14:34.906
But that is not what the Bible says.

16
01:14:34.906 --> 01:14:38.906
If the Bible does not say that it happens there, then it did not happen there either.

17
01:14:38.906 --> 01:14:44.906
In the Gospel of Matthew, Jesus says to his disciples, go to Galilee,

18
01:14:44.906 --> 01:14:45.906
that is all the way in the north.

19
01:14:45.906 --> 01:14:49.906
Go to Galilee, for there I will meet you when I have risen.

20
01:14:49.906 --> 01:14:56.906
So in Jerusalem, Jesus is crucified and then he rises from the dead.

21
01:14:56.906 --> 01:15:00.906
and then he says, before he is crucified, he says to his disciples,

22
01:15:00.906 --> 01:15:04.906
make sure you go to Galilee, for there I will meet you.

23
01:15:04.906 --> 01:15:08.906
That is the prophecy of Jesus himself about his death and his resurrection.

24
01:15:08.906 --> 01:15:13.906
And in Galilee, why does Jesus take his disciples back to Galilee?

25
01:15:13.906 --> 01:15:16.906
Why don't we just stay in Jerusalem, you might say?

26
01:15:16.906 --> 01:15:19.906
Actually, the best comment I can make about that is,

27
01:15:19.906 --> 01:15:24.906
the ministry of Jesus and his disciples began in Galilee.

28
01:15:24.906 --> 01:15:26.906
That is where it all started.

29
01:15:26.906 --> 01:15:31.906
And Jesus actually takes them back to Galilee and there he says,

30
01:15:31.906 --> 01:15:35.906
guys, this is where it began, this is where you did Bible college with me,

31
01:15:35.906 --> 01:15:40.906
here I taught you what it means to be a disciple of Jesus.

32
01:15:40.906 --> 01:15:45.906
And from this point, Jesus says, I no longer call you disciples, but I call you friends.

33
01:15:45.906 --> 01:15:50.906
And at this point he says, now go and make all nations my disciples.

34
01:15:50.906 --> 01:15:54.906
Then they go back to Jerusalem, so it's a bit of a back and forth,

35
01:15:54.906 --> 01:15:56.906
and that's why you also need forty days for that.

36
01:15:56.906 --> 01:15:59.906
It was no longer by car, but it was on foot.

37
01:15:59.906 --> 01:16:03.906
And so it was a back and forth, and so Jesus really needed those forty days

38
01:16:03.906 --> 01:16:06.906
to take a tour with his disciples.

39
01:16:06.906 --> 01:16:09.906
And then in Acts chapter 1 verse 8 it says,

40
01:16:09.906 --> 01:16:13.906
but you will receive the Holy Spirit, he will give you power,

41
01:16:13.906 --> 01:16:18.906
then you will tell people what you have seen and heard from me.

42
01:16:18.906 --> 01:16:23.906
First in Jerusalem, then throughout Judea and Samaria, and afterwards to the whole world.

43
01:16:23.906 --> 01:16:28.906
And in that passage it says that Jesus ascends into heaven.

44
01:16:28.906 --> 01:16:31.906
And the disciples are standing there watching like this.

45
01:16:31.906 --> 01:16:37.906
Dude, I would also be standing there thinking, what?

46
01:16:37.906 --> 01:16:40.906
I mean, you saw him die on the cross.

47
01:16:40.906 --> 01:16:42.906
That is credibly very sad.

48
01:16:42.906 --> 01:16:44.906
Then he rises from the dead.

49
01:16:44.906 --> 01:16:45.906
That is wow.

50
01:16:45.906 --> 01:16:48.906
Just like Thomas, I would probably have thought to myself,

51
01:16:48.906 --> 01:16:50.906
if I don't see it, then I have a hard time with that.

52
01:16:50.906 --> 01:16:53.906
But we have God's Word, amen, thank you.

53
01:16:53.906 --> 01:16:56.906
And then he goes to heaven and the angels say,

54
01:16:56.906 --> 01:16:59.906
why are you standing there looking up at heaven?

55
01:16:59.906 --> 01:17:06.906
This is the Jesus who said he would go, and this same Jesus will return.

56
01:17:06.906 --> 01:17:11.906
And today I want to talk about Matthew chapter 28 verse 19.

57
01:17:11.906 --> 01:17:14.906
If you have your Bible, take that Bible verse with you.

58
01:17:14.906 --> 01:17:17.906
Matthew chapter 28 verse 19.

59
01:17:17.906 --> 01:17:24.906
And it says, go now on your way, for one of the last things Jesus did at the end of his ministry,

60
01:17:24.906 --> 01:17:29.906
was to pass on his ministry to the people who follow him.

61
01:17:29.906 --> 01:17:31.906
And this is the great commission.

62
01:17:31.906 --> 01:17:37.906
And the great commission is also known as the subject of evangelism.

63
01:17:37.906 --> 01:17:42.906
And I want to talk today about the subject of evangelism.

64
01:17:42.906 --> 01:17:48.906
Recently, I have been having more and more conversations in Open Church with people, believing people in Open Church,

65
01:17:48.906 --> 01:17:53.906
who ask me, Tim, how does evangelism work in Open Church?

66
01:17:53.906 --> 01:17:55.906
What can we do? How can we approach it?

67
01:17:55.906 --> 01:18:01.906
Some people feel a kind of urge within them to go out on the street and talk about Jesus.

68
01:18:01.906 --> 01:18:04.906
I would say, I won't stop you, go for it.

69
01:18:04.906 --> 01:18:09.906
And some people ask, is there a team in Open Church, how we can evangelize together?

70
01:18:09.906 --> 01:18:15.906
And actually, it has become somewhat of a church thing in the past hundred years,

71
01:18:15.906 --> 01:18:23.906
that we have formed teams in the church and that we as a church community do a kind of evangelism as a church.

72
01:18:23.906 --> 01:18:32.906
But I want to provide insight today that evangelism is so much more than what we as a church are used to,

73
01:18:32.906 --> 01:18:37.906
for example, to agree as a church, on that Saturday we come together with twenty people,

74
01:18:37.906 --> 01:18:41.906
we go out on the street with a stage, we sing and people walk by, we hand out flyers,

75
01:18:41.906 --> 01:18:47.906
everyone wears a polo with a logo of Open Church, Jesus loves you and that is then evangelism.

76
01:18:47.906 --> 01:18:51.906
But that is not necessarily all that evangelism is.

77
01:18:51.906 --> 01:18:57.906
First, I want to say this, evangelism is the Greek word evangelion

78
01:18:57.906 --> 01:19:04.906
and it simply means the statement, the good message, that Jesus is Savior and Lord.

79
01:19:05.906 --> 01:19:11.906
Evangelism does not necessarily mean forcing people to come to repentance,

80
01:19:11.906 --> 01:19:14.906
because you cannot force people to come to repentance.

81
01:19:14.906 --> 01:19:16.906
That is indeed a change of heart.

82
01:19:16.906 --> 01:19:20.906
That comes from hearing the Word and from the work of the Holy Spirit.

83
01:19:20.906 --> 01:19:23.906
We cannot beat people into repentance.

84
01:19:23.906 --> 01:19:26.906
You cannot bring people to repentance with force.

85
01:19:26.906 --> 01:19:29.906
You cannot force people to love someone.

86
01:19:29.906 --> 01:19:33.906
That does not work in the world of love, and it does not work in the world of faith either.

87
01:19:33.906 --> 01:19:36.906
You cannot force anyone to come to Jesus.

88
01:19:36.906 --> 01:19:38.906
It must be a change of heart.

89
01:19:38.906 --> 01:19:46.906
But evangelism, the word evangelion from Greek, is the Greek word for evangelism

90
01:19:46.906 --> 01:19:50.906
and it means the good news that Jesus is Savior and Lord.

91
01:19:50.906 --> 01:19:51.906
That is the good news.

92
01:19:51.906 --> 01:19:59.906
And today I want to provide insight into evangelism and I want to give you six points if you have a notebook with you.

93
01:19:59.906 --> 01:20:02.906
I would like to encourage you to take some notes.

94
01:20:02.906 --> 01:20:07.906
Because, here comes that dear church, that everyone, a lot of information.

95
01:20:07.906 --> 01:20:10.906
I want to give you an assignment during this sermon.

96
01:20:10.906 --> 01:20:12.906
Listen carefully to what I am about to say.

97
01:20:14.906 --> 01:20:20.906
The six methodologies that I will explain, very briefly, the methodology and the Bible verse that is attached to it.

98
01:20:20.906 --> 01:20:23.906
Those six points that I will distribute.

99
01:20:23.906 --> 01:20:33.906
I want you to listen afterwards and assess for yourself whether this might be a ministry that God has given you.

100
01:20:33.906 --> 01:20:37.906
How do you know that God is calling you to something?

101
01:20:37.906 --> 01:20:41.906
You hear that when you have a resonance in your heart.

102
01:20:41.906 --> 01:20:45.906
That you think, yes, I am already doing this and I find it so great.

103
01:20:45.906 --> 01:20:51.906
Or, you think to yourself, yes, this is what keeps me awake at night.

104
01:20:51.906 --> 01:20:55.906
This is what occupies me, this must happen.

105
01:20:55.906 --> 01:21:01.906
Then it is indeed the Holy Spirit who has called you to do something specific in God's kingdom.

106
01:21:01.906 --> 01:21:05.906
And from those six points, I want to share two things with you.

107
01:21:05.906 --> 01:21:09.906
One, look at who you already are.

108
01:21:09.906 --> 01:21:17.906
And two, look at which of these things you can still grow in.

109
01:21:17.906 --> 01:21:18.906
That is also important.

110
01:21:18.906 --> 01:21:29.906
Because on the one hand, it is true that God wants to use you and that resonates in your spirit and that you are excited about it and find it wonderful already.

111
01:21:29.906 --> 01:21:36.906
On the other hand, it is also true that God sometimes calls us to enter into a challenge with Him.

112
01:21:36.906 --> 01:21:46.906
Namely, that we must crucify our flesh and say, yes, but my comfort in Christ is actually not what Jesus has called me for.

113
01:21:46.906 --> 01:21:52.906
But God challenges me to step out in faith, no matter what it costs.

114
01:21:52.906 --> 01:21:53.906
Do you understand what I mean?

115
01:21:53.906 --> 01:21:56.906
So here are the assignments. One, what are you already doing?

116
01:21:56.906 --> 01:21:59.906
And two, where can you learn and grow?

117
01:21:59.906 --> 01:22:03.906
And I was working on this sermon this week and I was excited.

118
01:22:03.906 --> 01:22:06.906
I also told Vanessa, I am really excited about this sermon.

119
01:22:06.906 --> 01:22:12.906
To be able to provide insight into what evangelism can also be in your personal life.

120
01:22:12.906 --> 01:22:17.906
I personally call evangelism personal evangelism.

121
01:22:17.906 --> 01:22:24.906
There is a word that I picked up during my training, and that is really what I have taken for myself, personal evangelism.

122
01:22:24.906 --> 01:22:27.906
I know for myself that I am an evangelist.

123
01:22:27.906 --> 01:22:33.906
I don't keep my mouth shut in the gym, not in the drugstore, I talk everywhere.

124
01:22:33.906 --> 01:22:42.906
But it has to be, I think, for myself, and that is my personal evangelism, it has to be a Holy Spirit moment.

125
01:22:42.906 --> 01:22:48.906
I'm not just going to someone standing at the checkout, hey, hey, hey, hey, hey, Jesus, Jesus, that's annoying.

126
01:22:48.906 --> 01:22:51.906
And Jesus didn't do that either, in my opinion.

127
01:22:51.906 --> 01:22:55.906
Jesus had Holy Spirit appointments.

128
01:22:56.906 --> 01:23:03.906
Jesus takes a detour through Samaria to meet someone with whom he actually had nothing to do.

129
01:23:03.906 --> 01:23:05.906
Those are Holy Spirit moments.

130
01:23:05.906 --> 01:23:10.906
And my heart's desire is that I can have Holy Spirit moments every time.

131
01:23:10.906 --> 01:23:13.906
That I can meet someone, and this can also be your prayer.

132
01:23:13.906 --> 01:23:15.906
Pray this once in a while, here is a tip.

133
01:23:15.906 --> 01:23:23.906
Pray once in a while, Lord, bring me to someone today whom I can bring closer to You.

134
01:23:23.906 --> 01:23:26.906
That is a beautiful prayer and God certainly agrees with it.

135
01:23:26.906 --> 01:23:32.906
And when I was preparing this week, last night I was sitting on the couch with Vanessa just chilling.

136
01:23:32.906 --> 01:23:37.906
And we were on the laptop, watching the revival conference.

137
01:23:37.906 --> 01:23:41.906
And did you know that there is a revival conference going on?

138
01:23:41.906 --> 01:23:43.906
Give a wave if you know about it.

139
01:23:43.906 --> 01:23:45.906
Yes, quite a few people.

140
01:23:45.906 --> 01:23:53.906
And I saw a piece that was exactly what I mean.

141
01:23:53.906 --> 01:23:58.906
And so I'm going to show you a video that lasts ten minutes of what I'm going to show you.

142
01:23:58.906 --> 01:24:02.906
Actually, that sermon lasts thirty minutes, but from those thirty minutes, I'm going to give you ten minutes.

143
01:24:02.906 --> 01:24:06.906
Normally, I don't show a video longer than five minutes.

144
01:24:06.906 --> 01:24:09.906
But I couldn't cut this piece.

145
01:24:09.906 --> 01:24:11.906
I couldn't help but say, well, that's where I stop.

146
01:24:11.906 --> 01:24:14.906
Because the next thing he said is also super important.

147
01:24:14.906 --> 01:24:19.906
What you are about to see is one of the leaders of YWAM, Youth With A Mission.

148
01:24:19.906 --> 01:24:23.906
And he is an evangelist at heart and soul.

149
01:24:23.906 --> 01:24:29.906
And the six points that I will mention shortly, what he is, is an apostolic evangelist.

150
01:24:29.906 --> 01:24:37.906
And so I'm going to give you the word shortly, the title of what kind of evangelism this is and what these people do.

151
01:24:38.906 --> 01:24:44.906
But apostolic evangelism is what this man is at heart and soul.

152
01:24:44.906 --> 01:24:49.906
He has what Jesus says, go now and make all nations my disciples.

153
01:24:49.906 --> 01:24:53.906
Baptize them in the name of the Father and teach them to do everything.

154
01:24:53.906 --> 01:24:57.906
And Jesus says in Acts, really, go out now.

155
01:24:57.906 --> 01:25:03.906
First in Jerusalem, then in all Judea and Samaria, and then to the ends of the earth.

156
01:25:03.906 --> 01:25:08.906
So there are evangelists who are called to go into the world.

157
01:25:08.906 --> 01:25:13.906
To seek out places in the world where people do not yet know Jesus.

158
01:25:13.906 --> 01:25:17.906
And you would say that the whole world is globalized and that everyone knows Jesus.

159
01:25:17.906 --> 01:25:19.906
That is not true at all.

160
01:25:19.906 --> 01:25:23.906
There are very large areas in the world that do not believe in Jesus at all.

161
01:25:23.906 --> 01:25:30.906
I had a friend in Australia and that guy went on a mission trip to Japan, to Tokyo.

162
01:25:30.906 --> 01:25:34.906
And in Tokyo he explained the gospel.

163
01:25:34.906 --> 01:25:38.906
And many people in Japan don't even know the name of Jesus.

164
01:25:38.906 --> 01:25:44.906
At least the West European people know the name Jesus, even if it's just as a curse word for them.

165
01:25:44.906 --> 01:25:48.906
But at least they know the narrative of Jesus a little bit.

166
01:25:48.906 --> 01:25:51.906
Almost everyone knows Jesus, both positively and negatively.

167
01:25:51.906 --> 01:25:54.906
But that is just the effect of Jesus.

168
01:25:54.906 --> 01:25:59.906
But in Japan there are many people who can't even pronounce Jesus because they have never heard of Him.

169
01:25:59.906 --> 01:26:02.906
And there are many areas in the world like this.

170
01:26:02.906 --> 01:26:05.906
And this is what Jesus says about evangelism.

171
01:26:05.906 --> 01:26:09.906
This is the first form of evangelism we see in the Bible.

172
01:26:09.906 --> 01:26:12.906
Apostolic evangelism.

173
01:26:12.906 --> 01:26:14.906
What does the word apostle mean?

174
01:26:14.906 --> 01:26:17.906
An apostle is someone who is sent out.

175
01:26:17.906 --> 01:26:21.906
Because first, the disciples were the students of Jesus.

176
01:26:21.906 --> 01:26:24.906
And from students, they eventually become apostles.

177
01:26:24.906 --> 01:26:26.906
There has been a switch.

178
01:26:26.906 --> 01:26:28.906
They are students of Jesus.

179
01:26:28.906 --> 01:26:32.906
And in a certain way, Jesus says, and now I send you out.

180
01:26:32.906 --> 01:26:34.906
From student to apostle.

181
01:26:34.906 --> 01:26:37.906
From disciple they are now apostles.

182
01:26:37.906 --> 01:26:44.906
And apostolic evangelism are those people who become warm in their hearts.

183
01:26:44.906 --> 01:26:50.906
And who have a craving in their soul to say, I just cannot stay in Lommel.

184
01:26:50.906 --> 01:26:52.906
I must go out.

185
01:26:52.906 --> 01:26:54.906
I want to go into the world.

186
01:26:54.906 --> 01:26:57.906
Just like Michael there, he is just going, it was Iraq, right?

187
01:26:57.906 --> 01:27:00.906
Who does it now? Who is going to Iraq now?

188
01:27:00.906 --> 01:27:03.906
But he goes to Iraq to explain the gospel.

189
01:27:03.906 --> 01:27:06.906
And that is apostolic evangelism.

190
01:27:06.906 --> 01:27:13.906
I was busy with this and I will please you in the next 10 minutes with the testimonies of this man.

191
01:27:13.906 --> 01:27:14.906
Great.

192
01:27:14.906 --> 01:27:18.906
You may turn off the lights and then we will watch a piece of film.

193
01:27:18.906 --> 01:27:19.906
So enjoy.

194
01:27:19.906 --> 01:27:21.906
I was very happy with it.

195
01:27:22.906 --> 01:27:25.906
God is at work all over the world.

196
01:27:25.906 --> 01:27:33.906
And through the work I do and the travels I make, I get opportunities to hear and see all kinds of things that God is doing.

197
01:27:33.906 --> 01:27:36.906
Last year I was in a country called Papua New Guinea.

198
01:27:36.906 --> 01:27:38.906
And we had a team there.

199
01:27:38.906 --> 01:27:44.906
And someone there told us that there was an unreached village somewhere deep in the interior, in a valley.

200
01:27:44.906 --> 01:27:49.906
No way to make contact with them, but we had heard that there were people there.

201
01:27:49.906 --> 01:27:54.906
And a team from our base said okay, we will go find them and bring the gospel.

202
01:27:54.906 --> 01:27:57.906
And they took a boat, spending a day on the boat.

203
01:27:57.906 --> 01:28:01.906
Then paddled a long river with a canoe.

204
01:28:01.906 --> 01:28:05.906
Then they hiked through the mountains, walking and walking.

205
01:28:05.906 --> 01:28:09.906
And they came into a large valley and there they saw a small village with people.

206
01:28:09.906 --> 01:28:15.906
And when they entered the village, there was immediately all kinds of commotion in the village.

207
01:28:15.906 --> 01:28:19.906
And people started talking and shouting and running around.

208
01:28:19.906 --> 01:28:22.906
And our team thought, guys, what is going on here?

209
01:28:22.906 --> 01:28:29.906
And what turned out was that years ago, before World War II, more than 80 years ago.

210
01:28:29.906 --> 01:28:33.906
A German couple of missionaries had gone to the village.

211
01:28:33.906 --> 01:28:35.906
To bring the gospel.

212
01:28:35.906 --> 01:28:39.906
And the people in that village had then killed and eaten the missionaries.

213
01:28:39.906 --> 01:28:41.906
They were cannibals.

214
01:28:41.906 --> 01:28:47.906
And when they had eaten the missionaries, they saw that the missionaries had Bibles with them.

215
01:28:47.906 --> 01:28:51.906
And then they realized, these were probably not people we should have eaten.

216
01:28:51.906 --> 01:28:56.906
These were people who served God and they felt terrible and so guilty.

217
01:28:56.906 --> 01:29:00.906
And they thought, surely God is very angry with us.

218
01:29:00.906 --> 01:29:04.906
And then they made the decision that the next missionaries who would come.

219
01:29:04.906 --> 01:29:08.906
That they would ask for forgiveness and make amends.

220
01:29:08.906 --> 01:29:11.906
And would listen to the message of the missionaries.

221
01:29:11.906 --> 01:29:15.906
And for more than 80 years, the people in that village waited.

222
01:29:15.906 --> 01:29:18.906
And one generation died and the new one arose.

223
01:29:18.906 --> 01:29:20.906
And the story was told and retold.

224
01:29:20.906 --> 01:29:23.906
Until our team entered the village.

225
01:29:23.906 --> 01:29:27.906
And they were the next missionaries to visit that village.

226
01:29:27.906 --> 01:29:29.906
And the whole village gathered.

227
01:29:29.906 --> 01:29:32.906
And the leaders of the village, the chief and the elders.

228
01:29:32.906 --> 01:29:35.906
They officially offered their apologies.

229
01:29:35.906 --> 01:29:38.906
And they said, we want to hear what you have to tell us.

230
01:29:38.906 --> 01:29:40.906
And the team brought the gospel.

231
01:29:40.906 --> 01:29:42.906
And everywhere people began to cry.

232
01:29:42.906 --> 01:29:44.906
And God's presence came.

233
01:29:44.906 --> 01:29:47.906
And people came to faith throughout the village.

234
01:29:47.906 --> 01:29:52.906
It was so fantastic how God moves and works in Papua New Guinea.

235
01:29:52.906 --> 01:29:54.906
And we see it happening in various places there.

236
01:29:54.906 --> 01:29:58.906
Shortly after that, I went to a country in the Middle East, a Muslim country.

237
01:29:58.906 --> 01:30:00.906
And I visited a hospital.

238
01:30:00.906 --> 01:30:03.906
And this hospital was started by missionaries.

239
01:30:03.906 --> 01:30:10.906
And in this hospital, the current king of the country was born.

240
01:30:10.906 --> 01:30:13.906
And several of his sons.

241
01:30:13.906 --> 01:30:20.906
And because they were born there, the missionaries have permission to turn it into a Christian hospital.

242
01:30:20.906 --> 01:30:24.906
And when you enter the hospital, there is a gigantic Bible verse on the wall.

243
01:30:24.906 --> 01:30:26.906
And everywhere there are Bibles.

244
01:30:27.906 --> 01:30:32.906
It is the only place in the entire region where you can pick up free Bibles.

245
01:30:32.906 --> 01:30:39.906
And when the missionaries started that hospital, the child mortality rate was 50%.

246
01:30:39.906 --> 01:30:46.906
So of all the children and all the babies that were born, half died immediately at birth, during delivery.

247
01:30:46.906 --> 01:30:50.906
And when the missionaries began to work there, the statistics started to change.

248
01:30:50.906 --> 01:30:55.906
And the hospital decided to specialize in premature babies.

249
01:30:55.906 --> 01:31:00.906
And they led us to the department where the babies were who were born far too early.

250
01:31:00.906 --> 01:31:07.906
And then they told us about the statistics, the history of child mortality and how different it is now.

251
01:31:07.906 --> 01:31:17.906
And then they said that this hospital is currently specialized in caring for unborn, for prematurely born babies.

252
01:31:17.906 --> 01:31:23.906
And that they have the highest survival rate of any hospital in the world.

253
01:31:24.906 --> 01:31:33.906
Babies who are born prematurely in that hospital literally have twice the chance compared to any other hospital in any Western country in the world.

254
01:31:33.906 --> 01:31:37.906
And then the missionary said to me, do you know why that is and how that can be?

255
01:31:37.906 --> 01:31:46.906
No, I don't know. He said, we have good doctors, we have good equipment, but the real difference is that room over there.

256
01:31:46.906 --> 01:31:49.906
He said, come with me. And he showed me a room.

257
01:31:49.906 --> 01:31:57.906
He says, here, prayer is happening 24 hours a day. Day and night, prayers are offered for the babies in the hospital.

258
01:31:57.906 --> 01:32:02.906
And God is working in a hospital in the Middle East.

259
01:32:02.906 --> 01:32:10.906
Then I was in Iran and believe it or not, but the fastest growing church in the world is in Iran.

260
01:32:10.906 --> 01:32:14.906
The fastest growing church in the world. God is at work in the Middle East.

261
01:32:15.906 --> 01:32:19.906
Last December I was at a conference in Brazil.

262
01:32:19.906 --> 01:32:24.906
And Brazil is next level. It is incredible what God is doing in Brazil.

263
01:32:24.906 --> 01:32:30.906
The hunger for God among young people, the passion in worship is unprecedented.

264
01:32:30.906 --> 01:32:33.906
It is truly absolutely a national revival.

265
01:32:33.906 --> 01:32:38.906
A few years ago we decided to organize a large gathering.

266
01:32:38.906 --> 01:32:41.906
In collaboration with several other organizations.

267
01:32:41.906 --> 01:32:45.906
And we rented a stadium to call young people to come.

268
01:32:45.906 --> 01:32:47.906
And to challenge them to live completely for God.

269
01:32:47.906 --> 01:32:51.906
And to give their lives to Him and be willing to go into missions.

270
01:32:51.906 --> 01:32:55.906
And we had rented a stadium that could hold 50,000 young people.

271
01:32:55.906 --> 01:32:57.906
And we weren't sure if we would fill it.

272
01:32:57.906 --> 01:33:03.906
But registration opened and within 24 hours every ticket was sold.

273
01:33:03.906 --> 01:33:08.906
And then we got thousands of people on the waiting list and thought maybe we should rent another stadium.

274
01:33:08.906 --> 01:33:10.906
So we rented another stadium in the same city.

275
01:33:10.906 --> 01:33:14.906
And in no time that stadium was sold out as well.

276
01:33:14.906 --> 01:33:18.906
Then we rented a third stadium and that was sold out too.

277
01:33:18.906 --> 01:33:20.906
And then we had three stadiums at the same time.

278
01:33:20.906 --> 01:33:28.906
150,000 young Brazilians seeking God for 12 hours in prayer and worship.

279
01:33:28.906 --> 01:33:30.906
And giving their lives to Jesus.

280
01:33:30.906 --> 01:33:34.906
And being willing to go wherever He sends them.

281
01:33:34.906 --> 01:33:39.906
It is incredible the movement of God in Brazil.

282
01:33:42.906 --> 01:33:44.906
Not long after, I was in Kenya.

283
01:33:44.906 --> 01:33:46.906
A country in East Africa.

284
01:33:46.906 --> 01:33:48.906
What is close to my heart.

285
01:33:48.906 --> 01:33:50.906
My wife and I lived there for eight years.

286
01:33:50.906 --> 01:33:52.906
Two of our children were born there.

287
01:33:52.906 --> 01:33:54.906
And friends of mine lead a youth ministry there.

288
01:33:54.906 --> 01:34:00.906
And they said, Daniel, in the past nine months, God is doing something among the youth here.

289
01:34:00.906 --> 01:34:06.906
We have seen 180,000 young people come to faith in the past nine months.

290
01:34:06.906 --> 01:34:08.906
180,000 young people!

291
01:34:09.906 --> 01:34:13.906
Africa is a continent full of young people.

292
01:34:13.906 --> 01:34:17.906
And there are enormous movements of God happening in Africa.

293
01:34:17.906 --> 01:34:19.906
And it is truly incredible.

294
01:34:19.906 --> 01:34:22.906
Whole schools coming to faith.

295
01:34:23.906 --> 01:34:25.906
But it is not only in Africa.

296
01:34:25.906 --> 01:34:28.906
We also see fantastic things in America.

297
01:34:28.906 --> 01:34:35.906
Since the 1980s, we have witnessed a decline in the number of Christians in America.

298
01:34:35.906 --> 01:34:36.906
In North America.

299
01:34:36.906 --> 01:34:37.906
Until now.

300
01:34:38.906 --> 01:34:41.906
In recent years, there has been a turnaround.

301
01:34:41.906 --> 01:34:44.906
And faith is increasing again in America.

302
01:34:44.906 --> 01:34:45.906
The churches are growing again.

303
01:34:45.906 --> 01:34:47.906
More and more people are coming to faith.

304
01:34:47.906 --> 01:34:51.906
And it is the youth in America who are changing the statistics.

305
01:34:51.906 --> 01:34:54.906
It is young people who are coming to faith.

306
01:34:54.906 --> 01:34:56.906
Young people who are returning to the church.

307
01:34:56.906 --> 01:35:01.906
In America, the sale of Bibles has increased by 22%.

308
01:35:02.906 --> 01:35:06.906
And one of the things that stands out the most about the growth of the church in America...

309
01:35:06.906 --> 01:35:10.906
is that it is being driven, it is being directed by young men.

310
01:35:10.906 --> 01:35:15.906
For the first time in a very long time, there are more men in the church in America than women.

311
01:35:15.906 --> 01:35:18.906
For years it was the women.

312
01:35:18.906 --> 01:35:21.906
And God is doing something among the men.

313
01:35:21.906 --> 01:35:22.906
Where are the men?

314
01:35:28.906 --> 01:35:29.906
There are the men.

315
01:35:30.906 --> 01:35:33.906
But it is not happening only in North America.

316
01:35:33.906 --> 01:35:36.906
God is also at work in Europe.

317
01:35:36.906 --> 01:35:38.906
God is also at work in Europe.

318
01:35:40.906 --> 01:35:41.906
Sweden.

319
01:35:41.906 --> 01:35:46.906
Sweden is known worldwide as one of the most secular countries in the world.

320
01:35:46.906 --> 01:35:50.906
And a few months ago, a large-scale survey was conducted...

321
01:35:50.906 --> 01:35:53.906
among thousands of Swedes through one of the national broadcasters.

322
01:35:53.906 --> 01:35:56.906
And the question that was asked to the people was...

323
01:35:56.906 --> 01:36:03.906
who do you think will be the most influential person in the year 2025?

324
01:36:03.906 --> 01:36:08.906
Who do you think will become the influencer of the year in 2025?

325
01:36:09.906 --> 01:36:11.906
And they wondered, would it be an athlete?

326
01:36:11.906 --> 01:36:13.906
Would it be a political leader?

327
01:36:13.906 --> 01:36:15.906
Would it be an actor?

328
01:36:15.906 --> 01:36:18.906
Could it perhaps be a social media influencer?

329
01:36:18.906 --> 01:36:21.906
And the results of the survey came back.

330
01:36:21.906 --> 01:36:23.906
And the answer was Jesus.

331
01:36:29.906 --> 01:36:31.906
So people in Sweden said...

332
01:36:31.906 --> 01:36:37.906
we expect that Jesus will be the most influential person of this year.

333
01:36:38.906 --> 01:36:40.906
And one of the reasons they gave for that...

334
01:36:40.906 --> 01:36:45.906
was because so many young people in Sweden are coming to faith.

335
01:36:45.906 --> 01:36:48.906
God is at work among the youth in Sweden.

336
01:36:50.906 --> 01:36:56.906
In Norway, because right next to it, a very large article came out...

337
01:36:56.906 --> 01:36:59.906
and the headline above the article read...

338
01:36:59.906 --> 01:37:02.906
atheism has had its day.

339
01:37:03.906 --> 01:37:05.906
Atheism is over.

340
01:37:06.906 --> 01:37:13.906
In the United Kingdom, the sale of Bibles has increased by 87% since 2019.

341
01:37:15.906 --> 01:37:21.906
And publishers of the Bible attribute the increase to the spirituality of Gen Z.

342
01:37:22.906 --> 01:37:26.906
Gen Z who finds strength in the Word of God...

343
01:37:26.906 --> 01:37:28.906
in the midst of uncertain times.

344
01:37:28.906 --> 01:37:33.906
The decline in church attendance in England has not only stopped...

345
01:37:33.906 --> 01:37:35.906
it has reversed.

346
01:37:35.906 --> 01:37:39.906
And the church in England is growing, is increasing.

347
01:37:41.906 --> 01:37:46.906
And it is Gen Z in England that is responsible for the difference.

348
01:37:47.906 --> 01:37:50.906
Moreover, in England, the percentage of Gen Z...

349
01:37:50.906 --> 01:37:53.906
that goes to church has quadrupled in the past year.

350
01:37:54.906 --> 01:37:58.906
And for young men, it has even grown five times as much.

351
01:37:59.906 --> 01:38:05.906
Yes, God is also at work among the men in England.

352
01:38:10.906 --> 01:38:12.906
He was.

353
01:38:19.906 --> 01:38:21.906
Powerpreka.

354
01:38:22.906 --> 01:38:26.906
And also the number of registrations for revival conferences...

355
01:38:26.906 --> 01:38:29.906
has increased in the past few years.

356
01:38:29.906 --> 01:38:34.906
And the number of people watching online is on the rise.

357
01:38:34.906 --> 01:38:36.906
And here is one thing, church.

358
01:38:36.906 --> 01:38:38.906
May I turn the light on a little in the room?

359
01:38:38.906 --> 01:38:39.906
Here is one thing, church.

360
01:38:39.906 --> 01:38:41.906
And I mean that seriously.

361
01:38:41.906 --> 01:38:43.906
I regularly talk about this with Vanessa.

362
01:38:43.906 --> 01:38:46.906
I really think that open church needs to prepare itself...

363
01:38:46.906 --> 01:38:49.906
with more and more people coming to repentance.

364
01:38:49.906 --> 01:38:52.906
And coming to repentance means...

365
01:38:52.906 --> 01:38:55.906
I believe that the new building we are going to build...

366
01:38:55.906 --> 01:38:57.906
is not luxury, but that it is necessary.

367
01:38:57.906 --> 01:39:01.906
Because we as a church need to catch the people who are coming to faith...

368
01:39:01.906 --> 01:39:04.906
and disciple them.

369
01:39:04.906 --> 01:39:06.906
They need to learn about the love of Jesus.

370
01:39:06.906 --> 01:39:09.906
Because coming to repentance is just one thing.

371
01:39:09.906 --> 01:39:11.906
That's amazing, isn't it? Your salvation forever.

372
01:39:11.906 --> 01:39:12.906
That's one thing.

373
01:39:12.906 --> 01:39:15.906
But discipleship after repentance is vital.

374
01:39:16.906 --> 01:39:20.906
If you don't clearly tell them after bringing the Word of God...

375
01:39:20.906 --> 01:39:22.906
how they should set their lives...

376
01:39:22.906 --> 01:39:24.906
then you get that effect of those four seeds.

377
01:39:24.906 --> 01:39:29.906
Seed on the rocks, seed on the path, seed among thorns and thistles...

378
01:39:29.906 --> 01:39:31.906
and seed in good soil.

379
01:39:31.906 --> 01:39:36.906
And you want to ensure as a church that people can sow the Word of God...

380
01:39:36.906 --> 01:39:39.906
in people's lives, but that it is also watered.

381
01:39:39.906 --> 01:39:42.906
That it is also directed and that it is taught.

382
01:39:42.906 --> 01:39:48.906
How do you now live from your old life, now that you have become a new creation...

383
01:39:48.906 --> 01:39:50.906
how do you now continue to live together with God?

384
01:39:50.906 --> 01:39:54.906
And there, Open Church is vital for the area in which we are.

385
01:39:54.906 --> 01:39:56.906
That is what we are working on.

386
01:39:56.906 --> 01:40:00.906
So I seriously believe that building the new building...

387
01:40:00.906 --> 01:40:03.906
is simply vital, simply necessary.

388
01:40:03.906 --> 01:40:05.906
So let's go for it.

389
01:40:05.906 --> 01:40:11.906
In any case, evangelism can be that you think to yourself...

390
01:40:11.906 --> 01:40:16.906
okay, I need to go out into the world to evangelize.

391
01:40:16.906 --> 01:40:20.906
But even if we all thought that, then Open Church would be empty, then Lommel would be empty...

392
01:40:20.906 --> 01:40:24.906
and then everyone would be eaten by cannibals in Papua New Guinea.

393
01:40:24.906 --> 01:40:25.906
That doesn't help.

394
01:40:25.906 --> 01:40:28.906
I can still imagine those cannibals like this...

395
01:40:28.906 --> 01:40:30.906
We shouldn't have eaten them.

396
01:40:30.906 --> 01:40:32.906
It's really such a strange story, isn't it?

397
01:40:32.906 --> 01:40:37.906
And I've heard it more often, even in Hilson there were people going to Papua New Guinea...

398
01:40:38.906 --> 01:40:43.906
and indeed, cannibalism is still a real threat even to this day.

399
01:40:43.906 --> 01:40:46.906
So you are also... Yes, it shouldn't happen anymore, I understand.

400
01:40:46.906 --> 01:40:48.906
It shouldn't happen anymore.

401
01:40:51.906 --> 01:40:53.906
Hey, that's not allowed, is it?

402
01:40:55.906 --> 01:40:57.906
But really such a story.

403
01:40:59.906 --> 01:41:03.906
And can you imagine those people coming to say sorry...

404
01:41:03.906 --> 01:41:07.906
Yeah, sorry, right. Because last time we had eaten those people.

405
01:41:10.906 --> 01:41:14.906
It's forgiven. I'm going to stand here, you know. Really such a crazy story.

406
01:41:14.906 --> 01:41:16.906
Cannibals, not normal.

407
01:41:16.906 --> 01:41:21.906
But people can't all be apostolic evangelists.

408
01:41:21.906 --> 01:41:25.906
So my question to you is, who are you as an evangelist?

409
01:41:25.906 --> 01:41:28.906
Because the Bible does say that we are all called...

410
01:41:28.906 --> 01:41:31.906
to proclaim the gospel of Jesus Christ.

411
01:41:31.906 --> 01:41:34.906
Whether it's to our family, whether it's to our friends, whether it's to our neighbors...

412
01:41:34.906 --> 01:41:38.906
whether it's to our colleagues, but we are all called...

413
01:41:38.906 --> 01:41:40.906
to tell the good news to the people around us.

414
01:41:40.906 --> 01:41:44.906
Here's a catch. If you don't do it, who will?

415
01:41:44.906 --> 01:41:47.906
If you don't do it to your brother or sister, who will?

416
01:41:47.906 --> 01:41:51.906
If you don't do it to your colleagues, why do you think you work where you work?

417
01:41:51.906 --> 01:41:54.906
Do you think you work where you work just to earn money and that's it?

418
01:41:54.906 --> 01:41:57.906
That's too small a life. Vanessa and I were just talking about that yesterday.

419
01:41:57.906 --> 01:41:59.906
That would be too small a life.

420
01:41:59.906 --> 01:42:04.906
You are not born to be born, to grow up, to work, and to die.

421
01:42:04.906 --> 01:42:08.906
There is more than that. Solomon speaks about this in the book of Ecclesiastes.

422
01:42:08.906 --> 01:42:11.906
There is more than that. We need to look to God. Amen?

423
01:42:11.906 --> 01:42:16.906
So apostolic or missionary evangelism is what we have just seen...

424
01:42:16.906 --> 01:42:21.906
based on Matthew chapter 28 verse 19. Are you such a person?

425
01:42:21.906 --> 01:42:24.906
Raise your hand if you have ever been on a mission trip.

426
01:42:24.906 --> 01:42:27.906
Raise your hand. Mission trip.

427
01:42:27.906 --> 01:42:32.906
A little higher, then we can see them. Super cool. Mission trip.

428
01:42:32.906 --> 01:42:35.906
Thank you on behalf of Jesus for doing this.

429
01:42:35.906 --> 01:42:40.906
And I actually want to advise everyone in the church as well...

430
01:42:40.906 --> 01:42:46.906
that if you have completely set your life, you don't have to be continuously on a mission trip...

431
01:42:46.906 --> 01:42:50.906
but it is healthy to go on a mission trip once in a while.

432
01:42:50.906 --> 01:42:53.906
Go to Romania once. Go to Hungary once.

433
01:42:53.906 --> 01:42:56.906
Go to the Middle East once. Go to South America once.

434
01:42:56.906 --> 01:42:59.906
Do it together with the Holy Spirit.

435
01:42:59.906 --> 01:43:03.906
Please, do not do things on your own initiative for which God has not given you clearance.

436
01:43:03.906 --> 01:43:06.906
Because if you go to Papua New...

437
01:43:06.906 --> 01:43:11.906
...Guinea without God giving you clearance...

438
01:43:11.906 --> 01:43:15.906
there is always a measure of grace and protection for the things you need to do.

439
01:43:15.906 --> 01:43:22.906
So if you just go to the red-light district of Prague on your own initiative...

440
01:43:22.906 --> 01:43:28.906
and you have not been called, who says that you are strong enough to confront the demonic powers in that area.

441
01:43:28.906 --> 01:43:31.906
So you should always do things together with God.

442
01:43:31.906 --> 01:43:35.906
Do you have a heart's desire for France? There is one like that...

443
01:43:35.906 --> 01:43:39.906
then you get a heart's desire for it. And the first thing you do is bring it to God.

444
01:43:39.906 --> 01:43:41.906
Here I have to do this.

445
01:43:41.906 --> 01:43:45.906
When I had just come to faith and was no longer taking pills...

446
01:43:45.906 --> 01:43:47.906
and was no longer doing stupid things in my life...

447
01:43:47.906 --> 01:43:52.906
back then during the time of Mysteryland and Tunderdome, there were always those red buses...

448
01:43:52.906 --> 01:43:54.906
and they parked in front of such a party.

449
01:43:54.906 --> 01:43:59.906
Nowadays they call that festivals, that's a nice word, we used to call that grapper parties.

450
01:43:59.906 --> 01:44:02.906
And there was a bus in front of it...

451
01:44:02.906 --> 01:44:07.906
and there were people who were proclaiming the gospel to those bald pill men.

452
01:44:07.906 --> 01:44:11.906
And I thought when I had just come to faith, you know what, I'm going to do that too.

453
01:44:11.906 --> 01:44:14.906
I'm going to get in that red bus, I'm going to proclaim the gospel of God too.

454
01:44:14.906 --> 01:44:18.906
And just before I wanted to go, because I had actually already figured out the organization...

455
01:44:18.906 --> 01:44:21.906
I had actually called once and I was actually planning to go...

456
01:44:21.906 --> 01:44:25.906
and just before I went, I felt, it wasn't a clear voice...

457
01:44:25.906 --> 01:44:27.906
but I felt very clearly that God said don't do it.

458
01:44:27.906 --> 01:44:29.906
Don't do it, Tim. Why?

459
01:44:29.906 --> 01:44:32.906
Because I might have been too weak in the flesh for it.

460
01:44:32.906 --> 01:44:36.906
Who knows? You should always discuss everything with God.

461
01:44:36.906 --> 01:44:38.906
Do you understand what I mean?

462
01:44:38.906 --> 01:44:42.906
So apostolic or missionary evangelism, you could call it that.

463
01:44:42.906 --> 01:44:47.906
There is another form of evangelism that is very important, which the Bible points to.

464
01:44:47.906 --> 01:44:52.906
You may write down the word, lifestyle evangelism.

465
01:44:52.906 --> 01:44:54.906
Lifestyle evangelism.

466
